
================================================================================================
A. M_j(E) as a relation-supported sum:  M_j = K_j(N), N=sum_s b_s, expanded in J(A,E).
================================================================================================
  K_j(N) for N=sum of 6 indicators b_s: expand K_j as poly in elementary symmetrics e_r(b)=S_r.
  Since b_s in {0,1}: e_r(b)=#{A:|A|=r, all b_s=1}=sum_{|A|=r} prod_{s in A} b_s, E[that]=S_r.
  So M_j = sum_r [K_j as poly in e_r] ... but cleaner: M_j=sum_r m_jr S_r with m from part(A) earlier.
  E=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]...: M_1..4=[2.7918367346938777, 6.1210884353741495, 5.779591836734694, 3.8054421768707485]  identity M_j=sum m_jr S_r(from J): True
  E=[0, 1, 3, 7, 12, 20]...: M_1..4=[2.0691403834260975, 0.6729746444032159, -1.609400123685838, -1.2075448361162646]  identity M_j=sum m_jr S_r(from J): True
  E=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]...: M_1..4=[3.2374149659863947, 7.364625850340136, 7.680272108843537, 5.247619047619048]  identity M_j=sum m_jr S_r(from J): True

