================================================================================================
D. Relaxed Delsarte LP: max L_y over prob vectors p with consec's tail-coupling.
================================================================================================
  THM-536 coupling: for E subset {0..maxE}, N_E >= N_{AP} pointwise is the WRONG-k story.
  Same-k relaxation tested: max sum_j c_j M_j(p) over p>=0, sum p=1, with the binding
  moment constraints that hold for ALL same-k E.  We use the achievable (M_2,M_4) box from
  the exhaustive window as the cone, and confirm the LP vertex is consec.
  k=8: L_y(consec) = c_0 + c_2 M_2 + c_4 M_4 = 1/16 + 1/40*6.1211 + 3/80*3.8054
        = 0.358231 = 2633/7350
  Since M_2 AND M_4 are SIMULTANEOUSLY maximized at consec (verified), and c_2,c_4>0,
  the separable upper bound c_0+c_2 max M_2 + c_4 max M_4 is ATTAINED at consec.
  => the Delsarte LP optimum over the realizable region EQUALS L_y(consec) for k=8.

DONE.
